; c05-setter-partner-holds-winner. Anchor: shot-0066 (Ch. 5).
; Printed: 2/3 (two to one).
; Claim: the tile that wins the bidder's off trick sits with one of the two
;   setters. Ambiguous. Read before the deal, among the three hands other
;   than the bidder's, it is 2/3 (that is c07-straight-off-double's
;   relation). Read from the setter who must play first and cannot follow,
;   so does not hold it, it is his partner's: this query.
; State: the bidder leads his off; the viewer is the next seat, holding no
;   tile of the led suit; the bidder's six and the other two hands' seven
;   are dealt uniformly.
; Exact: 7/20; 1/2 if the setter also knows the bidder lacks it. Book model:
;   1/3 (or 1/2).
(query
  (viewer v)
  (partner v p)
  (led-context q)
  (double d)
  (in d q)
  (holds p d))
